{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "b8f5a6d9-cda1-843c-8107-b4e27da34698",
  "created_at": "2026-01-08T09:50:16-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Terrence Hanlon",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:47:34-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:47:37-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, good morning. My name is Terrence Hanlon. I am calling about my recycling. The bin was not emptied, and there is a tag on it. The tag says rejected."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:47:47-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, rejected. Let me get your address and I'll see what I can tell you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:47:52-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is 304 Mill Street. Up on the Hill. And this is the second miss in a row, so two weeks now, nothing picked up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:48:00-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Two pickups in a row, okay. Did the tag say why? There's usually a box checked or a note on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:48:07-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there is a box checked. It says, um, contamination, I think. But I do not understand this. I put in cans, paper, the plastic jugs. [pause] Hold still, please. Sorry, I am doing my daughter's hair for school, one moment."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:48:20-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, take your time. Mornings, right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:48:23-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Okay. So, what counts as contamination? I rinse everything. I do not put garbage in there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:48:29-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Usually it's things like plastic bags, food still stuck in containers, greasy pizza boxes, or something that isn't recyclable at all. Were your items loose in the bin, or bagged?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:48:39-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Bagged. In a black bag, a kitchen bag, so nothing blows away. Is that wrong? I thought the bag was the neat way."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:48:47-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That could be it. The crews can't see inside a closed bag, so they tend to reject it. Recycling needs to go in loose."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:48:55-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Loose. So no bag at all. The first time they also left a tag, but I thought it was a mistake, so I did the same again. Now I see."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:49:05-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That would explain both. Empty the bag into the bin, take the bag out, and put it out loose on your next pickup day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:49:13-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And the two weeks that are in the bin now? They stay there until next time?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:49:19-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, they'll collect it all next time if it's loose and clean. Don't put anything extra out beside the bin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:49:26-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And the paper, can it be in a paper bag? Or is that also, um, not allowed?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:49:32-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Honestly, I'd keep it all loose to be safe. If you want, I can have someone look at the schedule for your street and confirm which day it is."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:49:41-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, the day I know. It is every other Thursday. Hmm, or is it Friday for the Hill? I thought Thursday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:49:48-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me check. [pause] Mill Street, you're on the Friday route, so tomorrow might be the day, depending on the week."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:49:55-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Friday. Then I have been putting it out one day early. That is also not good, I think."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:50:01-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It shouldn't hurt, but it's best to put it out the morning of, or the night before. Tomorrow, then, loose."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:50:08-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, loose, tomorrow, no bag. I think I have it. Thank you very much."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-08T09:50:13-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Mr. Hanlon. Have a good day."
    }
  ],
